The logic for `task-36820beb` involves identifying diagonal connected components of non-background pixels. If a component has more than one pixel, the endpoints (pixels with exactly one diagonal neighbor within the component) extend along the diagonal direction away from the rest of the component until they hit another non-background pixel or the grid boundary. Isolated pixels or non-diagonal connections (like vertical adjacency) do not trigger extension.

